A trap whose thread another core stopped while the trap waited for the lock goes on as the thread's,
so the core keeps the turn of a thread that is not ready, and would make the call it trapped for.

Caught-by: fuzz-smp2
Report: the running thread is not runnable

diff --git a/kernel/core.c b/kernel/core.c
--- a/kernel/core.c
+++ b/kernel/core.c
@@ -172,7 +172,7 @@ void core_thread_gone(const struct thread *t)
 struct thread *core_trapped(void)
 {
     struct thread *t = core_self()->current;
-    if (t != NULL && t->state == THREAD_READY) {
+    if (t != NULL) {
         return t;
     }
     sched_run_next();
